  "findings": [
    "Neither crop intervention produces an accepted candidate. Cropping alone is insufficient on these two inputs under the unchanged classifier and ten-second fitter.",
    "Both outline-star crops fail on a small classified lower-edge region (4.25 and 4.5625 mm\u00b2); the main star is retained at 0.743125% and 0.850625% target error. The region appears along a noisy/glossy edge, but its physical identity is not established.",
    "The bauble saved automatic crop includes background and has one corner outside the image. Its classified frame is fragmented and the fit loses three regions; error is 4.3805859%. The historical crop produces a different 3+3 routing and 2.236875% error but still loses a small near-edge region.",
    "The historical bauble crop also discards three reviewed upper-frame material samples. Of the twenty-six original source samples, automatic classification gets 21 correct; historical classification gets 19 correct, 4 wrong and 3 outside crop. Thus lower target error is not evidence of a better full-motif reconstruction.",
    "The bauble classifier errors affect the red frame before solving. The existing red-white-mixture classifier is the next isolated comparison, with the fitter still consuming binary masks."
  ],
  "visualReview": "All four rectified photos, classified masks, independent exported renders and source-coordinate overlays inspected. Star contours remain rounded with imperfect contacts. Bauble masks lose most faint frame sections; corresponding reconstructions contain narrow seams and distorted surrounding regions. Missing features are marked in the review images.",
  "limits": [
    "No new automatic cropper run or improved automatic benchmark claimed.",
    "Scores across crops refer to different targets and coverage; sparse source-material observations help expose discarded/misclassified regions but are not dense ground truth.",
    "All returned geometry passes the nominal geometry/paper checks; none of the four passes the unchanged image/feature acceptance. No physical assembly or original cutting paths available."
  ],
